 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"It is only a little and we have enough and to spare, and it makes me glad to see my face in the mirror.\"",
  "[silence] O-lan says nothing.",
  "[action] Wang Lung buys a golden pin.",
  "[action] Wang Lung puts the pin in O-lan's hair.",
  "[action] (to O-lan) Wang Lung laughs, takes O-lan's face.",
  "[action] (to O-lan) Wang Lung and O-lan sit together.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Tomorrow I will tell her this,\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung thinks to himself.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"If I had had this gold I would have bought land and added it to the fields and then I would have bought her and made her my second wife, but now it is only this and I will give it to her as a sign that she shall not be beaten again.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung calls for O-lan, speaks to her.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"Come and see this, my woman, and tell me if it is not a fine thing. Now you are a woman of means, and you shall never again be beaten.\"",
  "[says] (to O-lan) Wang Lung asks O-lan if she will ever be beaten again.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"Do you think you will ever be beaten again,\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) O-lan smiles slightly.",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"Not again,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"I will give you another piece of gold and you can buy cloth and make a new coat for the little fool---\"",
  "[says] (to O-lan) Wang Lung expresses regret about his daughter's condition.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"It is a pity she is a fool,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"but it is better than never to have had a child at all.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung looks at O-lan and continues speaking."
